sg-session (0.1.0-34) unstable; urgency=medium

  * sg-settingsctl shutdown poweroff|reboot: what wine-sg 0241's
    ExitWindowsEx starts for Start's Shut down and Restart -- waits while the
    session's programs close (wineboot --end-session, at most 30 s), then
    systemctl poweroff|reboot. Start's Shut down did nothing before.
  * polkit: 50-stained-glass-power.rules lets a local, active user power off
    and restart even while the login screen's session exists (logind's
    -multiple-sessions actions), as Windows lets any user shut down a
    workstation.
  * test/settingsctl-test.py: the wait, both verbs, refusals, polkit's no.
    Found by the 2026-09-26 ISO QA pass.

