sg-session (0.1.0-19) unstable; urgency=medium

  * sg-sysinfo: the administrative tools' Linux side -- devices (Device
    Manager: PCI/USB/network/disks/sound/input/monitors/CPUs with drivers,
    kernel modules and sg-drivers' "no driver" recommendations), disks and
    volumes with drive letters and unallocated space (Disk Management),
    Stained Glass's systemd units (Services), local users and groups, Samba
    shares, a hardware/OS summary (System Information), processes and
    connections (Resource Monitor), cleanup categories (Disk Cleanup).
    Windows programs reach it through `sg-sysinfo --bridge`.
  * sg-sysinfod (socket-activated, root): the Stained Glass journal for
    anyone with a Windows session; mount, unmount, drive letters, format,
    Samba sessions and system cleanup for administrators, refusing the
    system disk and volumes in use.
  * Gate: test/sysinfo-test.py (in make lint).

